{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDReduction.D_of_cov_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDReduction.D_of_cov_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDReduction.lean#L41-L48","doc":"Packaged with the free-cumulant framing (#3959 follow-up): `T₃ ≤ 0` is equivalent to the\ncovariance `Cov ≤ 0`, itself equal (via the Kerov polynomial `Σ̂₃ = R₄ + R₂`, `E_Planch[R₄] = −k`)\nto `Cov_Planch(f^λ, R₄) ≤ 0`. Here `cov ≤ 0` stands for that kernel and `hlink : 6(W−E) = −4·cov`\nfor the exact identity after `T₂ = 0` and `T₃ = (3/(k)₃)·(k!·cov)`-type normalization is absorbed\ninto `cov`. Kept abstract: the combinatorial `T₁,…` live outside Mathlib's current reach. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDReduction.D_of_T3_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDReduction.D_of_T3_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDReduction.lean#L32-L39","doc":"**Character reduction of (D).** Given the exact moment identity `6(W − E) = T₁ − 4T₃ − 3T₂`,\nthe conjugation vanishing `T₂ = 0`, and `0 ≤ T₁ = Σ(f^λ)³`, the sub-lemma (D) `E ≤ W` follows from\nthe covariance kernel `T₃ ≤ 0`. So the last open input of the #3939 growth bound is exactly\n`T₃ ≤ 0` (`Cov_Planch(f^λ, Σ_□ c(□)²) ≤ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}